window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_b1-4e22d23d06babfd8"]={"key":"ny_b1-4e22d23d06babfd8","group":"ny_b1","uid":"4e22d23d06babfd8","rank":34,"title":"westmere audiometry vendor recommendation","occupation":"nurse_practitioners","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_b1","prompt":"You’re the occupational health nurse practitioner supporting Westmere Manufacturing in England, and I’m Isabel Vanterpool, the clinic lead. Westmere’s audiometry arrangement expires on 31 March 2025, and Joaquin Kilgore needs Kestrel Clinic’s—correction, our occupational health team’s—authorized recommendation by 4:00 p.m. on 18 February so procurement can place the replacement contract without interrupting surveillance. Please issue the recommendation on behalf of the team and record that the procurement status has changed from “clinical review pending” to “occupational health recommendation issued.” There are no attachments; use only the planning facts in this message and apply the position in England as at 15 February 2025. The population is 480 employees whose initial tests must be completed during a six-week campaign of 30 working days. For planning, assume retests equal 6% of initial tests and round any test volume up to a whole test. Westmere values paid production time at £38 per employee-hour. Marlowe Trading Company, the incumbent mobile provider, quotes a £4,800 mobilisation charge plus £78 for every completed test, including retests. Its unit can complete 52 tests per service day, each attendance takes an employee away from production for 0.5 hour, and a retest is offered on the next service day, on a 10-business-day cycle. The alternative fixed-booth provider is forty minutes from the plant and quotes £52 for every completed test, including retests, with no mobilisation charge. It offers 18 appointments per working day, each attendance requires 2.0 paid hours away from production including travel and check-in, and retests are available within three business days. Marlowe’s technicians already understand Westmere’s shift-release pattern and know which crews commonly require retest coordination, but that continuity is not a quoted service level and must not be assigned an invented cash value. The fixed provider is cheaper on its invoice and faster for individual retests; the mobile service removes much less production time. In this business, “cost per test” is routinely used to mean either the vendor’s invoiced cost or the loaded cost after production time, so pin down which meaning you use wherever the term appears and make the alternative meaning visible. A pilot, provider visit, workforce consultation, and fresh exposure review cannot be completed before Joaquin’s deadline, so the recommendation must be useful despite that limitation without pretending those checks occurred. Prepare `westmere_audiometry_vendor_recommendation.docx` and write it at the top level of the working directory. Keep it to no more than two pages and make it readable by Joaquin and other non-clinical managers. The memo must (1) give exactly one vendor recommendation; (2) include a 100-point scoring table comparing direct price, production-time impact, retest service, and continuity or implementation risk, with your chosen weights stated and totaling 100; (3) show enough calculation for the reader to audit test volume, direct cost, production hours, loaded cost, capacity, and the comparison between providers; (4) explain how the incumbent’s unpriced operational knowledge affected the score without presenting it as guaranteed or monetized; (5) state the material clinical-governance, employer-duty, and health-information safeguards that procurement must preserve, in plain language and without suggesting that vendor selection itself proves compliance; and (6) identify assumptions and evidence limitations briefly. Do not invent discounts, additional charges, test outcomes, service levels, legal approvals, or numerical benefits beyond the figures above. Use aggregate workforce information only—no employee names or individual results. End the memo on the single recommended decision, not on a list of next steps or a request for Joaquin to choose between the vendors.\n\n---\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `westmere_audiometry_vendor_recommendation.docx` — A concise occupational-health vendor recommendation memo with a scored comparison table and one final vendor decision. (Must be written to the top level of the working directory using the exact filename.; Must be no more than two rendered pages.; Must contain a 100-point scoring table covering the four requested comparison areas.; Must give exactly one vendor recommendation and end on that decision.; Must use only the numerical and operational facts stated in the request.; Must use aggregate workforce information and avoid individual health information.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/westmere_audiometry_vendor_recommendation.docx","bytes":39706,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/864b388aa424187c71c89ddd947b4b15ba6f73834d94b5ced2b492906e47d807.docx","sha256":"864b388aa424187c71c89ddd947b4b15ba6f73834d94b5ced2b492906e47d807","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"WESTMERE MANUFACTURING\nOccupational health decision memo  |  15 February 2025\nTo\nJoaquin Kilgore, Procurement\nFrom\nIsabel Vanterpool, Clinic Lead (on behalf of the occupational health team)\nSubject\nReplacement occupational audiometry arrangement (expires 31 March 2025)\nProcurement status\nClinical review pending  →  Occupational health recommendation issued\nDecision — appoint Marlowe Trading Company. Its invoice is higher, but production-time value makes its loaded cost lower, and incumbent familiarity reduces implementation risk. The fixed-booth provider is cheaper on invoice and offers quicker individual retests; those benefits do not outweigh the operational burden under the stated weights.\nPlanning basis and auditable costs. 480 initial tests × 6% = 28.8, rounded up to 29 retests; total = 509 completed test events. “Cost per test” below means vendor invoice cost per completed event (including retests); loaded cost separately adds paid production time at £38 per employee-hour.\nProvider\nVendor invoice\n(£; £/event)\nAbsence\n(hours)\nProduction value\n(£)\nLoaded cost\n(£; £/event)\nMarlowe mobile\n4,800 + 509×78 = 44,502\n£87.44/event\n509×0.5 = 254.5\n254.5×38 = 9,671\n54,173\n£106.43/event\nFixed booth\n509×52 = 26,468\n£52.00/event\n509×2.0 = 1,018\n1,018×38 = 38,684\n65,152\n£128.00/event\nInterpretation. The fixed provider saves £18,034 on vendor invoices, while Marlowe saves £10,979 on loaded cost (£65,152 − £54,173) and avoids 763.5 employee-hours of absence. Both fit the campaign assumptions: Marlowe needs 10 service days (10×52 = 520 capacity) on its 10-business-day cycle; fixed booth needs 29 working days (29×18 = 522, within 30 days and 540 maximum campaign capacity). The fixed option has less scheduling margin and a much larger release burden, although its retests are available within three business days versus Marlowe’s next service day.\n100-point decision score (0–10 scale; higher is better; weighted points = score ÷ 10 × weight)\nCriterion (weight)\nMarlowe\nscore\nMarlowe\npoints\nFixed booth\nscore\nFixed booth\npoints\nDirect price (25)\n4\n10.0\n10\n25.0\nProduction-time impact (35)\n10\n35.0\n3\n10.5\nRetest service (20)\n5\n10.0\n10\n20.0\nContinuity / implementation risk (20)\n9\n18.0\n6\n12.0\nTOTAL (100)\n—\n73.0\n—\n67.5\nWhy the continuity score is not money. Marlowe technicians already understand Westmere’s shift-release pattern and crews that commonly need retest coordination. I scored that as a qualitative continuity advantage (9/10 versus 6/10), not as a guaranteed service level or cash saving; no valid price was supplied for it. The fixed provider’s faster retest access is reflected in its 10/10 retest score.\nSafeguards that procurement must preserve (England, as at 15 February 2025).\n• Noise-risk assessment and the Control of Noise at Work Regulations 2005 determine whether surveillance is needed and how often; buying a contract alone does not prove compliance. Westmere retains responsibility for a suitable programme and acting on competent advice.\n• Keep competent occupational-health oversight of test quality, repeat testing, interpretation, worker communication, and referral/escalation of concerning results; the vendor is not a substitute for clinical governance.\n• Audiograms are confidential special-category health information. Restrict identifiable records to the clinical team; give managers only appropriate aggregate programme information or limited fitness advice. Contract for proportionate UK GDPR/Data Protection Act 2018 controls: clear controller/processor roles, purpose limitation, minimised data, secure transfer, access limits, retention/deletion rules, and breach responsibilities. Consent is not automatically the sole lawful basis.\nEvidence limits and assumptions. This desk-based recommendation uses only the quoted planning facts. No pilot, provider visit, workforce consultation, or fresh exposure review was completed before the deadline; figures assume all 509 events are completed at the quoted rates and attendance times. Contracting should preserve the safeguards above and verify supplied assumptions proportionately, without treating those checks as already done. Workforce information is aggregate only.\nRecommended decision: Westmere should appoint Marlowe Trading Company for the replacement audiometry arrangement.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The required DOCX exists at the exact top-level filename and is a valid, readable Word document.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Submitted file metadata and successful DOCX opening.","grader_hint":"Confirm `westmere_audiometry_vendor_recommendation.docx` is present at the submission root and can be parsed or opened without repair."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The complete memo renders to no more than two pages.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered page count.","grader_hint":"Render the DOCX with standard office software and count pages; all substantive content, including the scoring table, must fit within two pages."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo identifies Westmere Manufacturing, the audiometry contract decision, and Joaquin Kilgore as the non-clinical decision audience.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Memo addressee, subject, opening, or equivalent document text.","grader_hint":"Accept natural variations in memo formatting, but all three contextual elements must be explicit."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memo makes exactly one unambiguous recommendation: either Marlowe Trading Company or the fixed-booth provider, with no co-recommendation or invitation for the recipient to choose.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Recommendation statement and conclusion.","grader_hint":"Either provider can earn credit if the calculations, scoring, stated interpretation of cost, and rationale consistently support it. A split, provisional, or ‘either option’ conclusion does not earn credit."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The final substantive sentence states or restates the single vendor decision rather than ending with next steps, an open question, or a request for approval.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Last substantive sentence of the memo.","grader_hint":"Ignore a signature block or footer. Inspect the last substantive sentence and confirm it closes on the chosen vendor."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo records that procurement status changed from clinical review pending to occupational health recommendation issued.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Status line, decision record, or memo body.","grader_hint":"Wording may vary, but both the former and new status must be identifiable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"A scoring table visibly compares Marlowe Trading Company and the fixed-booth provider.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"An actual Word table or clearly structured tabular object in the DOCX.","grader_hint":"Confirm that both alternatives appear in a structured comparison, not merely in separate prose paragraphs."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The scoring table covers direct price, production-time impact, retest service, and continuity or implementation risk, and its disclosed criterion weights total exactly 100 points.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Criterion labels and weights in the scoring table.","grader_hint":"Synonymous labels are acceptable. Add the disclosed weights and require an exact total of 100."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The displayed criterion scores, weights, and provider totals are internally arithmetically consistent with the scoring method stated in the memo.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scoring table calculations and any scoring legend.","grader_hint":"Recalculate each weighted total using the memo’s own disclosed scale. Allow only ordinary display rounding of ±0.1 point."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The recommended provider is the provider with the stronger final result under the memo’s disclosed scoring system.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Provider totals and recommendation statement.","grader_hint":"Compare the scoring-table result with the named recommendation. If totals tie, the memo must disclose and apply a decision rule that produces the recommendation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Before or where it first uses “cost per test,” the memo defines whether that phrase means invoice-only cost or loaded cost including production time.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Definition, table note, or calculation label.","grader_hint":"The definition must precede or accompany interpretive use of the term; an unexplained number labeled only ‘cost per test’ is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The alternative meaning of “cost per test” remains visible through separate, unambiguous labels for vendor invoice cost and production-adjusted or loaded cost.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Financial comparison labels and explanatory text.","grader_hint":"Confirm a non-specialist cannot mistake the invoice figure for the loaded figure. Exact terminology is not required."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The planning volume is derived as 480 initial tests plus 29 retests, for 509 total test events.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Volume calculation in the table or supporting text.","grader_hint":"Check that 6% of 480 is rounded up from 28.8 to 29 and added to the 480 initial tests."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Marlowe’s direct vendor cost is shown as £44,502, within ±£1.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Direct-cost calculation for Marlowe.","grader_hint":"Expected relationship is £4,800 + 509 × £78 = £44,502."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The fixed-booth provider’s direct vendor cost is shown as £26,468, within ±£1.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Direct-cost calculation for the fixed provider.","grader_hint":"Expected relationship is 509 × £52 = £26,468."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Marlowe’s production absence is shown as 254.5 employee-hours, within ±0.1 hour.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Production-time calculation for Marlowe.","grader_hint":"Expected relationship is 509 test events × 0.5 hour."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The fixed-booth provider’s production absence is shown as 1,018 employee-hours, within ±0.1 hour.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Production-time calculation for the fixed provider.","grader_hint":"Expected relationship is 509 test events × 2.0 hours."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The production-time values equal the respective absence hours multiplied by £38 per employee-hour.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Monetized production-time calculations for both providers.","grader_hint":"Expected values are £9,671 for Marlowe and £38,684 for the fixed provider, each within ±£1."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Loaded cost equals direct vendor cost plus monetized production time for each provider.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Loaded-cost totals and supporting calculations.","grader_hint":"Expected loaded totals are £54,173 for Marlowe and £65,152 for the fixed provider, each within ±£2 because of possible displayed rounding."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo accurately distinguishes the fixed provider’s direct invoice advantage from Marlowe’s loaded-cost advantage.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Comparative financial statement or table.","grader_hint":"The fixed provider’s direct-cost advantage is £18,034 ±£2, while Marlowe’s loaded-cost advantage is £10,979 ±£3. Both directions must be correct even if differences are not explicitly printed."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Any per-test figures disclose their denominator and are mathematically consistent, whether the practitioner uses 509 test events or 480 initially screened employees.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Per-test labels, notes, and arithmetic.","grader_hint":"Accept either denominator if explicitly named and applied consistently. Recalculate values with a tolerance of ±£0.10 per test."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo tests campaign feasibility against capacity: Marlowe can accommodate 509 events in 10 service days at 52 per day, and the fixed provider can accommodate them within 30 working days at 18 per day.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Capacity calculation or feasibility statement.","grader_hint":"Accept equivalent calculations: Marlowe needs 10 rounded-up service days and has capacity for 520; the fixed provider needs 29 rounded-up working days and has capacity for 540."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The comparison interprets the fixed provider’s thinner capacity margin and larger employee-release burden as operational considerations without claiming either provider is infeasible.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Capacity and production-impact analysis.","grader_hint":"Both providers fit the supplied campaign assumptions. Look for a proportionate discussion of scheduling resilience rather than an unsupported failure claim."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Retest service is compared accurately as Marlowe’s next service day on a 10-business-day cycle versus the fixed provider’s availability within three business days.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Retest row and explanatory text.","grader_hint":"Both service facts and the fixed provider’s faster individual turnaround must be clear."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The incumbent’s familiarity with shift release and crew-level retest coordination is explicitly weighed as a continuity or implementation advantage.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Continuity-risk score and rationale.","grader_hint":"The factor must affect the reasoning or score, not appear as an isolated factual aside."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memo treats incumbent familiarity as unpriced and non-guaranteed, and does not convert it into invented savings, test quality, or turnaround performance.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Assumptions, limitations, and continuity discussion.","grader_hint":"Credit requires both restraint and disclosure: familiarity may be scored qualitatively, but it must not be represented as a contractual service level or unsupported numerical benefit."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The England compliance statement accurately explains that the need and frequency of occupational audiometry arise from noise-risk assessment and applicable health-surveillance duties, not merely from buying a vendor contract.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Clinical-governance or compliance section.","grader_hint":"Look for a materially accurate plain-language application of the Control of Noise at Work Regulations 2005 as at 15 February 2025. A detailed legal citation is optional."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memo states that Westmere retains responsibility for an adequate surveillance programme and cannot transfer that duty simply by appointing either provider.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Employer-duty statement.","grader_hint":"Equivalent wording is acceptable. The document must not imply that vendor selection alone establishes legal compliance."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memo preserves competent occupational-health oversight of test quality, repeat testing, interpretation, employee communication, and referral or escalation of concerning results.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Clinical-governance safeguards.","grader_hint":"These functions may be summarized compactly, but the memo should distinguish clinical oversight from simple appointment provision."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Audiometry results are recognized as confidential health information requiring restricted clinical access, with management receiving only appropriate aggregate or fitness-related information.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Information-governance safeguards.","grader_hint":"Look for clear separation between identifiable clinical results and non-clinical management reporting."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memo calls for proportionate UK data-protection contracting and controls, such as defined controller/processor roles, secure transfer, access limits, retention, and breach responsibilities, without asserting that consent is automatically the sole lawful basis.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Data-protection discussion.","grader_hint":"Assess against UK GDPR and Data Protection Act 2018 principles as at the stated date. Compact coverage is acceptable; unsupported claims that routine employee consent resolves all processing are not."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memo discloses that no pilot, provider visit, workforce consultation, or fresh exposure review was completed before the deadline and uses a defensible desk-based fallback rather than implying those checks occurred.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Assumptions and limitations statement.","grader_hint":"The fallback may be expressed as reliance on supplied quote assumptions with proportionate pre-contract verification, but it must not displace or hedge the present vendor recommendation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"All quantitative claims are traceable to the supplied figures or arithmetic derived from them; no discounts, extra charges, clinical outcome rates, service levels, or numerical value for familiarity are introduced.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Complete memo, scoring table, and footnotes.","grader_hint":"Audit every nontrivial number. Dates, page numbering, criterion scores, and correctly derived arithmetic are permitted; unsupported commercial or clinical quantities are not."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The recommendation explicitly reconciles the central tension between lower invoiced price, lower loaded operational cost, faster fixed-site retests, and incumbent continuity rather than relying on a single unqualified price figure.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Executive recommendation, scoring rationale, and conclusion.","grader_hint":"A defensible recommendation must acknowledge material evidence favoring the other provider and explain why the chosen weighting or cost interpretation controls the decision."},{"rubric_item_id":"R35","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo contains only aggregate workforce data and no employee names, individual audiometry findings, diagnoses, or crew-level health-result lists.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Full document text and embedded objects.","grader_hint":"Ordinary business contacts named in the request are allowed. Check that no synthetic individual clinical records were invented."},{"rubric_item_id":"R36","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The two-page memo is professionally usable by non-clinical managers: the decision is prominent, labels are unambiguous, the table is legible, calculations can be followed, and clinical or legal terminology is translated into plain language.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered memo as a whole.","grader_hint":"Judge the artifact as a real decision memo. Technically correct content should not earn this item if dense presentation, unexplained abbreviations, poor table scaling, or conflicting labels make it impractical to use."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"Westmere Manufacturing needs an occupational-health recommendation before its audiometry contract expires. The nurse practitioner is authorized to issue the team’s recommendation, balancing procurement cost, production disruption, retest access, clinical governance, and health-information safeguards for an English workplace.","difficulty_sources":["The lower invoice and the lower loaded operational cost point to different providers.","The fixed provider offers faster individual retests while the incumbent reduces production disruption and implementation risk.","Incumbent operational familiarity is relevant but unpriced, non-contractual, and unsuitable for invented monetization.","The phrase “cost per test” has two routine meanings that must be defined and used consistently.","The decision deadline prevents a pilot, site visit, workforce consultation, or fresh exposure review, requiring a transparent desk-based fallback.","The recommendation must remain clinically and legally restrained while being understandable to non-clinical managers."],"authoring_plan":{"reference_material":{"files_to_build":[],"instruction":"Do not create reference files. Every local commercial fact needed by the solver is embedded in the request; professional clinical and regulatory safeguards come from occupational knowledge."},"gold_derivations":{"planning_volume":{"initial_tests":480,"retest_rule":"Retests equal 6% of initial tests, and a fractional test is rounded up.","retests":29,"total_test_events":509},"marlowe":{"direct_cost_rule":"£4,800 mobilisation plus £78 multiplied by total test events.","direct_cost":44502,"production_hours_rule":"Total test events multiplied by 0.5 hour.","production_hours":254.5,"production_value_rule":"Production hours multiplied by £38.","production_value":9671,"loaded_cost_rule":"Direct cost plus production-time value.","loaded_cost":54173,"capacity_rule":"Divide 509 by 52 and round required service days up.","required_service_days":10,"available_capacity":520,"retest_service":"Next mobile service day on a 10-business-day cycle."},"fixed_booth":{"direct_cost_rule":"£52 multiplied by total test events.","direct_cost":26468,"production_hours_rule":"Total test events multiplied by 2.0 hours.","production_hours":1018,"production_value_rule":"Production hours multiplied by £38.","production_value":38684,"loaded_cost_rule":"Direct cost plus production-time value.","loaded_cost":65152,"capacity_rule":"Divide 509 by 18 and round required working days up.","required_working_days":29,"available_capacity_over_campaign":540,"retest_service":"Appointment within three business days."},"comparisons":{"fixed_direct_cost_advantage_rule":"Marlowe direct cost minus fixed-provider direct cost.","fixed_direct_cost_advantage":18034,"marlowe_loaded_cost_advantage_rule":"Fixed-provider loaded cost minus Marlowe loaded cost.","marlowe_loaded_cost_advantage":10979,"production_hours_avoided_by_marlowe":763.5},"per_test_interpretations":{"acceptable_denominators":["509 completed test events","480 initially screened employees"],"rule":"Any per-test or per-employee figure must state its denominator and remain consistent. The memo must separately identify invoice-only and loaded cost."}},"professional_rules_for_gold":["The Control of Noise at Work Regulations 2005 should be applied as an employer duty linked to risk assessment and exposure; a vendor appointment does not itself prove compliance or make annual audiometry universally mandatory.","The employer retains responsibility for arranging a suitable health-surveillance programme and acting on competent occupational-health advice.","Audiometry delivery requires competent test administration, quality control, repeat-test handling, clinical interpretation, communication with the worker, and proportionate referral or escalation.","Individual audiometry data are confidential special-category health data. Non-clinical managers should ordinarily receive aggregate programme information or appropriately limited fitness advice, not individual results.","UK GDPR and Data Protection Act 2018 controls should include a clear allocation of controller and processor roles as applicable, purpose limitation, data minimization, secure transfer, restricted access, retention controls, and breach responsibilities.","The memo should not claim that employee consent is invariably the sole lawful basis for occupational-health processing.","The incumbent’s knowledge of shift-release patterns and crew-level coordination is a legitimate continuity consideration but is not contractual, guaranteed, or monetizable from the supplied facts.","Both providers fit the stated campaign capacity assumptions. The fixed provider has less capacity margin and a much larger release burden; it should not be falsely described as mathematically incapable of completing the campaign.","The fixed provider has the lower invoice and faster individual retest availability. Marlowe has lower loaded cost, much lower production absence, and incumbent continuity. A high-quality decision acknowledges all four facts."],"solver_feasible_verdicts":{"preferred_reference_verdict":"Recommend Marlowe Trading Company because its higher invoice is more than offset by reduced production absence, giving the lower loaded cost, while incumbent operational familiarity reduces implementation risk.","alternate_acceptable_verdict":"Recommend the fixed-booth provider only if the memo deliberately gives controlling weight to invoice expenditure and rapid individual retest access, clearly acknowledges the higher loaded cost and production burden, and produces a scoring result consistent with that priority.","invalid_verdicts":["Naming both providers as co-recommendations.","Leaving the choice to Joaquin Kilgore.","Selecting a provider contrary to the displayed score without an explicit tie-break or reconciliation.","Treating cost per test as a single undefined figure.","Monetizing incumbent familiarity or inventing clinical outcomes."]},"document_fit_check":"A two-page solution is feasible using a short decision-led memo, one compact scoring and calculation table, and concise paragraphs for rationale, limitations, governance safeguards, status change, and conclusion. The rubric does not require separate sections for each item.","reachability_check":"All arithmetic uses figures in the request and can be reproduced offline. The clinical-governance, occupational-health, confidentiality, and England-specific regulatory expectations are standard practitioner knowledge. No private code, undisclosed template, live rate, or external source is required."},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"multi_artifact_bundle","structure":"freeform"},"reference_files":[],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"vendor_recommendation_memo","filename":"westmere_audiometry_vendor_recommendation.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"A concise occupational-health vendor recommendation memo with a scored comparison table and one final vendor decision.","required":true,"constraints":["Must be written to the top level of the working directory using the exact filename.","Must be no more than two rendered pages.","Must contain a 100-point scoring table covering the four requested comparison areas.","Must give exactly one vendor recommendation and end on that decision.","Must use only the numerical and operational facts stated in the request.","Must use aggregate workforce information and avoid individual health information."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"communicate_stakeholders","work_product":"clinical_administrative_package","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"professional_judgment"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"nurse_practitioners","sector":"healthcare_social_assistance","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":2.5,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"domain_expert","reviewer_policy":"One occupational-health reviewer should verify the clinical, privacy, and England-specific statements; one independent commercial reviewer should recalculate all volumes, costs, capacities, weights, and recommendation consistency. Either vendor outcome is acceptable only when the memo explicitly defines its interpretation of cost, applies a transparent 100-point model consistently, acknowledges contrary evidence, and ends with one decision.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["No vendor contracts, insurance certificates, data-processing schedules, quality records, site assessments, workforce consultation results, or current exposure assessment are supplied.","The recommendation is necessarily desk-based and may identify proportionate contractual verifications without claiming they have already occurred.","Incumbent familiarity is qualitatively relevant but cannot be assigned a validated financial or clinical effect from the available facts."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:41:02+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:41:02+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:41:02+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:41:02+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":false,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"instruction 与 rubric criterion 存在 8-gram 逐字重叠: ['R06', 'R08', 'R24']","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:41:02+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_b1/runs/4e22d23d06babfd8","declared_deliverables":["westmere_audiometry_vendor_recommendation.docx"]};
